.TH SWAYDESK-DESKTOP-CONFIG 1 2026-11-14 "swaydesk 0.1.0" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-desktop\-config \- read the desktop configuration and apply the accent color
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-desktop\-config
get KEY
.br
.B swaydesk\-desktop\-config
generate
.br
.B swaydesk\-desktop\-config
apply
.br
.B swaydesk\-desktop\-config
css
.br
.B swaydesk\-desktop\-config
setup
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads ~/.config/sway\-desktop/config.toml for the shell scripts and writes the files that depend on the accent color.
.PP
The session runs it under the name sway\-desktop\-config (a link in the package's helper directory to /usr/bin/swaydesk\-desktop\-config); the process name is sway\-desktop\-config too.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B get KEY
Print a value of the configuration; an unknown key exits 2.
.TP
.B generate
Write the files that depend on the color.
.TP
.B apply
Write the files and reload Sway.
.TP
.B css
Print the accent colors as GTK CSS (@define\-color).
.TP
.B setup
The first login in the packaged session: copy from the skeleton what is missing in the home folder, then generate.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exit 0 at once without doing anything: the Python launchers use it to check that the binary and its libraries load.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sway\-desktop/config.toml
The desktop configuration: language (locale), accent color (accent), GTK and icon themes (gtk_theme, icon_theme), folder color (folder_color), file manager (file_manager), weather location (weather_location) and holidays (holidays). The fonts come from the GTK system font.
.TP
.I /usr/share/swaydesk\-desktop/skel/
The skeleton that setup copies.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swaydesk (7),
.BR swaydesk\-theme (1)
